hadiths[300]{hadithnumber,text}:
"309","""Islam is pure, so remain pure, and indeed only a pure person will enter Paradise."""
"310","""The honor of a believer in the sight of Allah is in the cleanliness of his clothes."""
"311","""Islam is founded upon cleanliness."""
"312","""There is no harm in the urine of donkeys and animals whose meat is permissible to eat."""
"313","""The purity of the earth is its becoming dry."""
"314","""Two types of water are not sufficient for ghusl after janabah: sea water and bathhouse water."""
"315","""When the water reaches forty pitchers, it does not become impure."""
"316","""The earth becomes impure due to urine only after forty days."""
"317","""Dig up the place of this (urine) and pour water over it."""
"318","""It has been declared forbidden to enter the bathhouse without a lower garment (waistcloth)."""
"319","""If a cat puts its mouth into a utensil, it should be washed seven times."""
"320","""Do not urinate while standing."""
"321","""When one of you does not find water but finds nabidh, then he should perform ablution with that."""
"322","""Do not perform ablution in the toilet in which you urinate, for indeed the water of a believer's ablution will be weighed along with his other good deeds."""
"323","""Whoever shakes hands with a Jew or a Christian should perform ablution and wash his hand."""
"324","""Ablution upon ablution is light upon light."""
"325","""Whoever performs ablution despite already being in a state of purity, Allah Almighty writes ten good deeds for him."""
"326","""Whoever presented a vessel to his brother for ablution, it is as if he has presented him with a horse."""
"327","""Wudu is the key to prayer."""
"328","""The miswak increases a person in eloquence."""
"329","""Prayer with miswak is seventy times superior to prayer without miswak."""
"330","""Whoever recites Bismillah during ablution, two angels continuously write good deeds for him until his ablution is broken."""
"331","""Do the khilal (interlacing/cleansing) of the fingers during ablution; (by doing so) on the Day of Resurrection, fire will not do their khilal."""
"332","""When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ablution, he used to move his ring."""
"333","“Rinsing the mouth and putting water into the nose is Sunnah.”"
"334","""If someone forgets to wipe his head and remembers it during the prayer, if he finds moisture in his beard, he should wipe with it; this will suffice for him. But if he does not find moisture, he should repeat the prayer and ablution."""
"335","""(In a lengthy hadith it is mentioned that) the Prophet (peace be upon him) wiped his neck while performing ablution."""
"336","""Wiping the neck is a means of protection from the collar (of punishment) on the Day of Resurrection."""
"337","""When the Prophet (peace be upon him) washed his hands, he recited this supplication «بسم الله والحمد لله . . . » and when he washed his face, he recited this supplication «اللهم بيض وجهي . . . » ."""
"338","""Because of urine, the limbs of ablution should be washed once each; because of stool, twice each; and because of major impurity (janabah), three times each."""
"339","""I would prefer to cut off my feet rather than wipe over the leather socks (mash on the socks)."""
"340","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to wipe over the outer part of the socks by drawing lines with his fingers."""
"341","""(Ibn Abi Amarah, may Allah be pleased with him, asked, O Messenger of Allah!) Should I wipe over the socks? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes. He said: For one or two days, until he mentioned seven days; so the Prophet said: For as long as you find it suitable."""
"342","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to wipe over the bandages (of wounds)."""
"343","""When you perform ablution, sprinkle (water) under your garment."""
"344","""He performed ablution well and then raised his gaze towards the sky."""
"345","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had a cloth with which he used to dry his limbs after performing ablution."""
"346","""If someone vomits (during prayer), or has a nosebleed, or something from inside the stomach reaches the mouth, or experiences the emission of madhiy (pre-seminal fluid), then he should leave (the prayer) and perform ablution."""
"347","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) vomited and did not perform ablution."""
"348","""Whoever touches an idol should perform ablution."""
"349","""(In a lengthy narration it is mentioned that) the Prophet (peace be upon him) ordered that those who laughed (during prayer) should repeat their ablution and prayer."""
"350","""When someone laughs out loud, he should repeat his ablution and prayer."""
"351","""Once a man was offering prayer with his lower garment hanging below his ankles, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: Go and perform ablution."""
"352","“Ablution becomes obligatory due to that which comes out of the body, not due to that which enters the body.”"
"353","""Wudu is required for every flowing blood."""
"354","""There is a devil of ablution who is called Walhan, so beware of the whispers regarding water."""
"355","“Tayammum is that the hands are struck on the earth twice: once for the face and once for both hands up to the elbows.”"
"356","""The Sunnah is that a person should perform only one prayer with a single tayammum, and then perform tayammum again for another prayer."""
"357","""The one who performs tayammum should not lead those who have performed ablution in prayer."""
"358","""Whoever performs ghusl (ritual bath) due to janabah acquired through lawful means, Allah Almighty will grant him one hundred palaces of white pearls."""
"359","""Do not bathe with water heated by the sun because it causes leukoderma."""
"360","""Whoever bathes the deceased, conceals his faults, and fulfills the trust, Allah Almighty will forgive forty of his major sins."""
"361","""Whoever, due to impurity, leaves even a hair's breadth of space unwashed while performing ghusl, then with that part he will be dealt with in the Hellfire in such and such a manner."""
"362","""Under every hair there is impurity, so wash the hair and cleanse the skin."""
"363","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform ghusl (ritual bath) on Fridays, on the day of Eid al-Fitr, on the day of Eid al-Adha, and on the day of Arafah."""
"364","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform ghusl for four reasons: for Jumu'ah (Friday prayer), after sexual impurity (janabah), after cupping (hijama), and after washing a deceased person."""
"365","""Take a bath every Friday even if you have to buy water in exchange for your whole day's food."""
"366","""Whoever performed ablution after taking a bath is not one of us."""
"367","""A menstruating woman and a person in a state of major ritual impurity should not recite anything from the Noble Qur'an."""
"368","""The only thing that prevented the Prophet (peace be upon him) from reciting the Qur'an was the state of major ritual impurity (janabah)."""
"369","""The minimum duration of menstruation is three days and the maximum duration is ten days."""
"370","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prescribed forty days for women experiencing postnatal bleeding, unless they become pure before that."""
"371","""When the muezzin begins the call to prayer, the Lord places His hand on his head and remains so until the muezzin finishes the call."""
"372","""Only a person in a state of ablution should give the call to prayer (Adhan)."""
"373","""No child should give the call to prayer until he reaches puberty."""
"374","""Only an eloquent person should give the call to prayer (adhan) for you."""
"375","""Whoever, at the time when the muezzin says «اشهد ان محمدا رسول الله» , kisses the inner sides of both index fingers and passes them over his eyes, for him the intercession of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) will become obligatory."""
"376","""In the city where the call to prayer (Adhan) is frequent, the cold decreases."""
"377","""The muezzin of the inhabitants of the heavens is Jibreel (peace be upon him), and the imam is Mikaeel (peace be upon him)."""
"378","""The words of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to be repeated in the Adhan and the Iqamah."""
"379","""The one who gives the adhan should also say the iqamah."""
"380","""The muezzin has more authority over the adhan, while the imam has more authority over the iqamah."""
"381","""Whoever says only the Iqamah is not one of us."""
"382","""When Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) began to pronounce the Iqamah, when he reached «قد قامت الصلاة» , the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: «اقامها الله وادامها» ."""
"383","""Between every two calls to prayer (i.e., the adhan and the iqamah) there is (optional) prayer, except at Maghrib."""
"384","""Keep such an interval between your adhan and iqamah as would allow one who is eating or drinking to finish his food and drink."""
"385","""If a child is born to someone and he recites the adhan in the right ear and the iqamah in the left ear, then the disease of Umm Sibyan will not harm him."""
"386","""He who did not perform the prayer has no share in Islam."""
"387","""Allah Almighty first made prayer obligatory upon people regarding their religion."""
"388","""The one who safeguards prayer, fasting, and ritual purity from major impurity is a true friend (wali), while the one who neglects them is a true enemy."""
"389","""I have been forbidden from killing those who pray."""
"390","""Whoever performed the ‘Isha prayer in congregation has attained his share of Laylat al-Qadr."""
"391","""Neither should the prayer be delayed for food, nor for any other work."""
"392","""The earliest time of prayer is the pleasure of Allah, while the last time is a cause for Allah's forgiveness and pardon."""
"393","""Whoever illuminates the Fajr, Allah Almighty will illuminate his heart and grave, and his prayer will also be accepted."""
"394","""Brighten the Fajr and you will be forgiven."""
"395","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would perform the Fajr prayer when light had spread across the sky."""
"396","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) would delay the Asr prayer until the sun remained white and clear."""
"397","""Whoever engages in worldly talk in the mosque, Allah Almighty destroys his deeds."""
"398","""Every night a caller announces: O inhabitants of the graves! Whom do you envy? They reply: Those connected to the mosque (i.e., those who are associated with the mosques)."""
"399","""Protect your mosques from your children."""
"400","""Staying in mosques is the monasticism of my Ummah."""
"401","""Whoever lights a lamp in a mosque, the common angels and the angels who bear the Throne continue to seek forgiveness for him as long as the light of that lamp remains in the mosque."""
"402","“Take care of these mosques by whitewashing them, placing lamps in them, lighting lanterns, and applying pure fragrance.”"
"403","""On the Day of Resurrection, all the lands will perish except the mosques; they will join together with one another."""
"404","""Whoever sweeps any house of Allah (i.e., a mosque), it is as if he has performed Hajj four hundred times."""
"405","""Sweeping the mosques is the dowry of the houris of Paradise."""
"406","""The rewards of my Ummah were presented before me, even (including) the straw which a person removes from the mosque."""
"407","""If any of you finds a louse in the mosque, he should bury it."""
"408","""If the person offering prayer does not have a stick (or something similar as a sutrah), then he should draw a line."""
"409","""Nothing breaks the prayer, (therefore, keep away the passerby in front of you) as much as you are able."""
"410","""Whoever deliberately passes in front of someone who is praying will wish on the Day of Resurrection that he were a dry tree."""
"411","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) saw a man who was performing prayer using another man as a sutrah, so he ordered him to repeat the prayer."""
"412","""Beware! No person should perform prayer by taking another person or a grave as a sutrah."""
"413","Hazrat Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the last prayer which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed behind me, he performed it in a single garment."
"414","""It is Sunnah to offer prayer in a single garment."""
"415","(Abu Abdur Rahman says:) I saw the Prophet (peace be upon him) and Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) praying in a single garment; half of the garment was on the Prophet (peace be upon him) and half was on Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"416","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) forbade praying in trousers."""
"417","""When you pray, lift your garments above the ankles. Whatever part of your garments touches the ground is in the Fire."""
"418","""When you stand for prayer, wear your shoes."""
"419","""It is also part of the completion of prayer that one should pray while wearing shoes."""
"420","“Jibreel (peace be upon him) came to me, and he recited ‘Bismillah ir-Rahman ir-Raheem’ aloud at the beginning of the prayer.”"
"421","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to raise his hands at the beginning of the prayer, then he would not do so again."""
"422","""Whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would go into bowing (ruku') and rise from bowing, he would raise his hands. Then, he would raise his hands only at the beginning of the prayer and not at any other time."""
"423","""Whoever raised his hands in prayer, his prayer is not valid."""
"424","""It is Sunnah to place one hand over the other below the navel during prayer."""
"425","""The recitation of the Imam is the recitation for the one who has an Imam in front of him."""
"426","""The recitation of the Imam is sufficient for you, whether he recites quietly or aloud."""
"427","""There is no recitation behind the Imam."""
"428","""Whoever recites (Qur'an) behind the Imam, his prayer is not valid."""
"429","""I have remembered two pauses in the prayer: one pause (of silence) when the Imam says the opening Takbir until he begins the recitation, and one pause after completing Surah Al-Fatihah and another Surah before bowing (ruku’)."""
"430","""There are two pauses for the Imam; consider the recitation of Surah Al-Fatihah during them as a blessing."""
"431","""The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) recited «غير المغضوب عليهم ولا الضالين» , said Ameen, and lowered his voice with it."""
"432","""I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when he performed prostration, he would place both his knees on the ground before his hands."""
"433","""When any one of you bows (in ruku‘), he should say «سبحان ربي العظيم» three times in ruku‘, and when he prostrates (in sujud), he should say «سبحان ربي الاعليٰ » three times in sujud."""
"434","""Sajdah on the forehead is obligatory, while sajdah on the nose is voluntary."""
"435","""When a woman sits in prayer, she should place one thigh over the other, and when she prostrates, she should attach her belly to her thighs."""
"436","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to stand on the balls of both his feet during prayer."""
"437","""Whoever did not send blessings upon the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), his prayer is not accepted."""
"438","""When the Imam, after completing the prayer, sits and becomes without ablution before saying the salam, his prayer is complete."""
"439","""Whoever, after performing the morning prayer and before speaking any word, recites Surah Al-Ikhlas one hundred times, then whenever he recites 'Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad', the sins of his year are forgiven."""
"440","""Whoever combines two prayers without a valid excuse has committed a major sin."""
"441","""Surely, Allah Almighty does not accept the prayer of one who lets his lower garment hang below the ankles."""
"442","""There is no prayer for the one who looks here and there."""
"443","""Whoever looks here and there during prayer, Allah Almighty rejects his prayer."""
"444","""Placing the hand on the side during prayer is the comfort of the people of Hell."""
"445","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to touch his beard during prayer."""
"446","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade blowing during prostration."""
"447","""It is better for one of you to restrain his hand from pebbles (while in prostration) than to have a hundred she-camels."""
"448","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to wipe the sweat from his face during prayer."""
"449","""Sneezing, dozing, and yawning during prayer are from Satan."""
"450","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) disliked yawning during prayer."""
"451","""The one with the most handsome face should lead the people in prayer."""
"452","""If you wish that your prayers be accepted, then let your best people lead your prayers."""
"453","""Whoever prays behind a pious scholar, it is as if he has prayed behind a Prophet."""
"454","""Perform prayer behind every righteous and wicked person."""
"455","""Whoever led a people in prayer and then remembered that he was without ablution or in a state of impurity, then he should repeat his prayer and the followers should also repeat their prayer."""
"456","""After me, no one should ever lead the prayer while sitting."""
"457","""Place the Imam in the middle."""
"458","""Whoever offered the Fajr prayer in congregation, it is as if he performed fifty Hajj with Adam (peace be upon him)."""
"459","""Whoever does not miss a single rak'ah of Fajr prayer for forty days will see his place in Paradise before he dies."""
"460","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) always performed Qunoot in the Fajr prayer until he departed from this world."""
"461","""When a believer performs the obligatory prayer in congregation, his sins fall away from him just as these leaves fall."""
"462","""Two and more than that constitute a congregation."""
"463","""When the congregation stands, there is no prayer except the obligatory one, except for the two Sunnah of Fajr."""
"464","""Do not precede your Imam in bowing (ruku‘), for you will surely catch up with that which has preceded you."""
"465","""The time for the obligatory prayer arrived while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on our mounts. So he (peace and blessings be upon him) moved forward and led us in prayer, and we performed the prayer on our mounts."""
"466","""O Ali! Do not prompt the imam during the prayer."""
"467","""A woman by herself constitutes a (separate) row."""
"468","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would not abandon the Sunnah prayers of Fajr whether he was traveling or at home."""
"469","""Whoever offers four rak'ahs before Zuhr, all the sins of that day are forgiven for him."""
"470","""Whoever does not regularly perform four rak'ahs before Zuhr will not be granted my intercession."""
"471","""Whoever prays four rak'ahs before 'Asr, Allah Almighty makes his body forbidden for the Fire."""
"472","""Whoever offers six rak‘ahs after Maghrib and does not utter any bad words in them, then these rak‘ahs will be equal to twelve years of worship for him."""
"473","""Whoever prays twenty rak‘ahs between Maghrib and ‘Isha, Allah Almighty will build a house for him in Paradise."""
"474","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to offer two rak'ahs of prayer after Maghrib, and he would recite so long in them that (all) the people of the mosque would leave the mosque."""
"475","Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I had two times to present myself before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): one at night and the other during the day. When I would come to him at night (and he would be engaged in prayer), he would clear his throat to inform me of his presence."
"476","""The honor of a believer is in his standing (in prayer) at night."""
"477","""Two units of prayer in the middle of the night erase sins."""
"478","""The two rak‘ahs that the son of Adam performs in the last part of the night are better for him than the world and whatever is in it, and if it were not that I would place a burden on my ummah, I would have made these rak‘ahs obligatory upon them."""
"479","""Never abandon the night prayer, even if you pray only as much as the time it takes to milk a goat."""
"480","""O people of the Qur'an! Do not make the Qur'an a pillow, and recite it during the hours of the day and night as it deserves to be recited."""
"481","""The one whose prayers are more during the night, his face is (equally) beautiful during the day."""
"482","""When any of you goes to sleep with the intention of performing Qiyam al-Layl, let him keep a handful of soil by his side."""
"483","""Allah Almighty has added another prayer to your prayers, and that is Witr."""
"484","""Whoever did not perform Witr is not from among us."""
"485","""The one who did not perform Witr, his prayer is not valid."""
"486","""Witr is obligatory upon the people of the Qur'an (i.e., the memorizers)."""
"487","""Witr is obligatory upon every Muslim."""
"488","""Witr prayer is three rak‘ahs like Maghrib."""
"489","""Whoever misses the Witr at night should make it up in the morning."""
"490","""The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to offer twenty rak‘ahs (units) of (Tarawih) prayer in Ramadan."""
"491","""During the time of Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), people used to perform twenty-three rak‘ahs of prayer (Tarawih) in Ramadan."""
"492","""Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered a man to lead the people in twenty rak‘ahs (units) of (Tarawih) prayer."""
"493","""Ibn Abi Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) used to lead the people of Madinah in twenty rak'ahs of prayer (Tarawih) during Ramadan."""
"494","""There is a gate in Paradise called Duha. Whoever performs the Duha prayer, on the Day of Resurrection this prayer will incline towards him just as a child inclines towards its mother, until it welcomes him, and the worshipper enters Paradise."""
"495","""There is a gate in Paradise called Duha; only the person who regularly performed the Duha (forenoon) prayer will enter through it."""
"496","""Whoever regularly performs the Duha prayer and does not abandon it without any reason or cause, then I and that person will ride on a boat of light in a sea of light in Paradise until we visit the Lord."""
"497","""A hypocrite does not perform the Duha (forenoon) prayer."""
"498","""Offer the Duha prayer with the two surahs of the same name: 'By the Sun and its brightness' (Ash-Shams) and 'By the forenoon' (Ad-Duha)."""
"499","""Whoever offers two units of the Duha prayer, Allah Almighty writes one hundred thousand good deeds for him."""
"500","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) would not abandon the Duha prayer even during travel and other circumstances."""
"501","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) would perform the Duha prayer to such an extent that we would say, 'Now he will never leave it,' and then he would leave it to such an extent that we would say, 'Now he will never perform it.'"""
"502","""Whoever has a need from Allah Almighty or from any of the sons of Adam, let him perform ablution and perform it well, then pray two units of prayer, then praise Allah Almighty, then send blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and then recite this supplication «لا اله الا الله الحليم . . . الا قضيتها يا ارحم الراحمين» """
"503","""O Messenger of Allah! What should a sinner do to repent from sins?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""He should take a bath after the Witr prayer on Monday night and perform twelve units of prayer."""
"504","""Whoever kept vigil on the night of Ashura (Muharram) with (optional prayers and acts of worship), it is as if he worshipped Allah in the manner of the inhabitants of the heavens."""
"505","""Whoever fasts on the first Thursday of Rajab, then on the night of Friday prays twelve rak‘ahs of prayer... (lengthy hadith regarding Salat al-Raghaib)."""
"506","""Whoever offered the Maghrib prayer on the first night of Rajab and then performed twenty units of prayer..."""
"507","""Whoever prays fourteen rak‘ahs on the night of the fifteenth of Rajab... Allah Almighty will send a thousand angels towards him."""
"508","""Whoever prays one hundred rak‘ahs of prayer on the night of mid-Sha‘ban... Allah Almighty will fulfill all his needs."""
"509","""Whoever prays two rak'ahs on the night of Friday, reciting Surah Al-Fatihah and Surah Az-Zalzalah fifteen times in each rak'ah, Allah Almighty will grant him protection from the torment of the grave and the terrors of the Day of Judgment."""
"510","""Whoever offers two rak'ahs between Zuhr and Asr on Friday... he will not depart from this world until he sees his Lord in a dream and his abode in Paradise."""
"511","""Whoever offers four rak'ahs of prayer on Saturday at the time of Duha... glad tidings are for them."""
"512","""Whoever prays four rak'ahs on Sunday night, reciting Surah Al-Fatihah once and Surah Al-Ikhlas fifteen times in each rak'ah, Allah Almighty will grant him on the Day of Resurrection the reward of reciting the Qur'an ten times and acting upon it ten times."""
"513","""Whoever offers four rak'ahs on Monday... Allah Almighty will grant him a palace in Paradise."""
"514","""The most virtuous day is the day of Friday."""
"515","""Jumu'ah is the Hajj of the poor."""
"516","""When the day of Friday is safe, then all the days are safe."""
"517","""The excellence of the Friday in Ramadan over the other Fridays is like the excellence of the month of Ramadan over all other months."""
"518","""Whoever misses the Friday prayer should give one dinar in charity."""
"519","""Taking a bath on Friday is Sunnah."""
"520","""Take a bath on Friday even if you have to buy a bowl of water for a dinar."""
"521","""Whoever cuts their nails and moustache every Friday, Allah Almighty will place healing in them and remove illness from them."""
"522","""The example of a believer on the day of Jumu'ah is like that of a person in the state of Ihram; he should neither cut his hair nor his nails until he has completed the prayer."""
"523","“Offering Friday prayer with a turban is seventy times more virtuous than offering Friday prayer without a turban.”"
"524","""There are some angels of Allah Almighty who seek forgiveness for those who wear white turbans on Friday."""
"525","""Jumu'ah is obligatory upon the one who spends the night with his family."""
"526","""Jumu'ah is obligatory upon the one to whom its call reaches."""
"527","""The established practice is that Jumu'ah is obligatory for every forty or more people."""
"528","""When seventy of us go for Friday prayer, they are like those seventy individuals who, in the form of a delegation, went with Musa (peace be upon him) to their Lord, or they are even better than them."""
"529","""Jumu'ah and Tashreeq are only in the city's central mosque."""
"530","""If there were no pulpits, the people of the settlements would have been burnt."""
"531","""When the Prophet (peace be upon him) would ascend the pulpit, he would say Salam (greet with peace)."""
"532","""When the preacher ascends the pulpit, neither prayer is valid nor conversation."""
"533","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform four rak'ahs before the Friday sermon, and he would not separate them (by concluding with salam) in any of them."""
"534","""Whoever speaks during the Friday sermon while the Imam is delivering the khutbah is like a donkey carrying books, and whoever says to him 'Be quiet,' his Friday (prayer) is not valid."""
"535","""Whoever jumps over people's necks after the Imam has entered the mosque and creates separation between two people is like one who is dragging his intestines in the fire of Hell."""
"536","""On the day of Friday, good deeds are doubled."""
"537","""Whoever recites these words three times before Fajr on Friday «استغفر الله الذى لا اله الا هو الحي القيوم واتوب اليه» , all his sins will be forgiven, even if they are as much as the foam of the sea."""
"538","""Whoever recites Surah Ha-Meem ad-Dukhan on the night of Friday will be forgiven."""
"539","""Whoever recites Surah Ha-Meem ad-Dukhan on the night of Friday or on Friday, Allah Almighty will build a house for him in Paradise."""
"540","""Whoever spends the nights of Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha in prayer, seeking reward from Allah Almighty, his heart will not die on the day when all hearts will die."""
"541","""Whoever prays one hundred rak‘ahs on the night of Eid al-Fitr... (long hadith)."""
"542","""We would eat, drink, and bathe (on the day of Eid al-Fitr), and then proceed towards the Eid prayer ground."""
"543","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to wear red sheets on the two Eids and on Fridays."""
"544","""Adorn your Eids with Takbeerat."""
"545","""Adorn the two Eids with Tahleel, Tahdees, Tahmeed, and Takbeer."""
"546","""Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say the takbeerat in such a loud voice that the people on the road would hear."""
"547","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to say four takbirs in the Eid prayers, just like the takbirs of the funeral prayer."""
"548","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) led the Eid prayer in two rak‘ahs and in them he recited only Surah Al-Fatihah."""
"549","""The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to recite 'Amma Yatasa'aloon' and 'Wash-Shamsi wa Duhaha' in the Eid prayers."""
"550","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) forbade wearing weapons in Islamic territories on the occasions of the two Eids, except if there is an enemy present (then it is not forbidden)."""
"551","""I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on the days of the two Eids, and there was a spear in front of him."""
"552","""On one Eid occasion, rain fell upon the people, so the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) led them in the Eid prayer inside the mosque."""
"553","""The best people of my Ummah are those who, when they travel, perform Qasr (shortened) prayers."""
"554","""O people of Makkah! Do not shorten the prayer for a distance less than four barid, such as the distance from Makkah to Usfan."""
"555","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to sometimes shorten the prayer during travel and sometimes offer it in full."""
"556","""Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said that I went with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) for Umrah in Ramadan, so he performed shortened prayers while I performed complete prayers. Then I said to him: You performed shortened prayers and I performed complete prayers. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Aisha! You have also done well."""
"557","""The one who offers full prayers during travel is like the one who shortens the prayer while at home."""
"558","""Whoever performs four rak‘ahs during a journey is like one who performs two rak‘ahs while at home."""
"559","""Whoever performs four rak‘ahs of prayer while on a journey should repeat the prayer."""
"560","""Do not shorten the prayer except during Hajj or Jihad."""
"561","""The time for the prayer of the one who forgets to pray is when he remembers it."""
"562","The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was asked about a person who forgets how many units of prayer he has performed during the prayer. He (peace be upon him) said: He should repeat the prayer and perform two prostrations while sitting."
"563","""There is no forgetfulness (sahw) in the prayer of fear."""
"564","""There are no prostrations of forgetfulness (sajda sahw) upon the follower behind the imam, but if the imam forgets, then both the imam and the follower must perform the prostrations of forgetfulness."""
"565","""When any one of you removes his shoes during prayer, he should not place them in front of him, for then he would be following them, nor should he place them behind him, for then one of his brothers might follow them; rather, he should place them between his feet."""
"566","""In each rak‘ah (unit) of the eclipse prayer, there is one bowing (rukū‘)."""
"567","""Was Surah Al-Hajj given superiority because it contains two prostrations?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Yes, and whoever does not perform both prostrations should not recite them."""
"568","""The prayer of the prisoner is two rak‘ahs until he dies or Allah frees him from captivity."""
"569","""The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) instructed Hazrat Ja'far (may Allah be pleased with him) to perform prayer standing on the boat, except if there is a fear of drowning (then permission is granted to pray while sitting)."""
"570","""Allah Almighty does not accept the prayer of three people, nor does any of their good deeds ascend to the heavens: a runaway slave until he returns to his masters; a woman whose husband is angry with her until he becomes pleased with her; and an intoxicated person until he regains his senses."""
"571","""Whoever becomes the guardian of an orphan should trade with his wealth and not leave it so that zakat consumes it."""
"572","""I asked, 'O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him),' about zakat, and he (peace be upon him) was asked about it. He (peace be upon him) said: 'Indeed, there is a (due) right in wealth other than zakat.' Then he (peace be upon him) recited this verse from Surah Al-Baqarah: 'Righteousness is not that you turn your faces towards the east or the west.'"""
"573","""One dinar of zakat is due on every grazing horse."""
"574","""There is no obligatory zakat in the intermediate amount (i.e., between two specified quantities)."""
"575","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to command us to pay zakat on trade goods."""
"576","""In cucumber, watermelon, pomegranate, sugarcane, and vegetables, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) has exempted zakat."""
"577","""There is no zakat on vegetables."""
"578","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered that grapes should be estimated in the same manner as dates are estimated, and their zakat should be collected in the form of dried raisins just as the zakat of dates is taken in the form of dried dates (i.e., chuwara)."""
"579","""There is no zakat on jewelry."""
"580","""When you estimate and assess the grain, then leave one third; if you cannot leave one third, then leave one fourth."""
"581","""There is no zakat in honey."""
"582","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) granted the mines of the place of Qabliyyah to Hazrat Bilal bin Harith Muzani (may Allah be pleased with him). This place is on one side of the location of Fara’. Thus, from these mines until today, nothing has been taken except for zakat."""
"583","""Zakat has never been mixed with any wealth except that it destroyed it."""
"584","""Pay Zakat and seek a knowledgeable person for it, because he is more pious and righteous."""
"585","""Soon there will come to you (those who collect zakat) such people whom you will dislike, but when they come to you, welcome them and let them collect zakat as they wish. If they act with justice and fairness, there will be reward, and if they act unjustly, the sin will be upon them. But you should keep them pleased, because the completion of your zakat lies in keeping them pleased, and they should supplicate for you."""
"586","""To collect grain from grain, goat from goats, camel from camels, and cow from cows."""
"587","""We said (to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him): 'The collectors of Zakat are unjust to us; can we hide our wealth equal to their excess?' He said: 'No.'"""
"588","""Regarding zakat, Allah Almighty was not pleased with the command of any prophet nor with the command of anyone else, until He Himself gave the command concerning it and divided the expenditures of zakat into eight categories."""
"589","""In Sadaqat al-Fitr, one sa' of wheat is on behalf of two individuals."""
"590","""On this (i.e., Eid) day, make the poor free from wandering door to door."""
"591","""The best charity is that a Muslim man learns knowledge and then teaches it to his Muslim brother."""
"592","""Shall I not tell you about the best charity? (It is that) your sister is returned to you (due to divorce or something similar) and she has no one to earn for her except you."""
"593","""Which charity is the best?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Charity given in Ramadan."""
"594","""Hasten in giving charity, for charity wards off trials."""
"595","""Even a small amount of charity wards off many calamities."""
"596","""A generous person is close to Allah's mercy, close to Paradise, close to people, and far from the fire of Hell, whereas a miser is far from Allah, far from Paradise, far from people, and close to Hell. And an ignorant generous person is more beloved to Allah Almighty than a miserly worshipper."""
"597","""Paradise is the home of generous people."""
"598","""The deceitful, the miserly, and the one who reminds others of his favors will not enter Paradise."""
"599","""Charity saves from a bad death."""
"600","""The poor are the towels of the rich; they cleanse their sins with them."""
"601","""Whoever's excuse becomes apparent, then charity becomes obligatory upon him."""
"602","""Give to the beggar even if he comes riding on a horse."""
"603","""If you must ask, then ask from righteous people."""
"604","""Only Paradise should be asked for by means of Allah's Essence."""
"605","""When an orphan cries, his tears fall upon the palm of the Most Merciful."""
"606","""Whoever gave water to drink at a place where he had control over the water, then for every sip of water he gave, there are ten good deeds for him, whether he is righteous or wicked."""
"607","""Kindness and gentle behavior towards people is also charity."""
"608","""Whoever does not have charity should curse the Jews."""
